# Except example data
!test_data/example*
!test/example*

# Files this repository must track despite the broad rules above.
#
# The blanket *.txt and *.log rules exist to keep Nextflow run output out of the
# tree. They also silently excluded requirements.txt -- which is why CI's
# "pip install -r requirements.txt" had never once succeeded -- and every caller
# result fixture under tests/fixtures (hla.result.txt, *.t1k.txt, time.log). The
# existing fixtures survive only because they were committed before the rule bit;
# a new one could not be added without -f.
!requirements.txt
!requirements-analysis.txt
!tests/fixtures/**

# Environment files
.env
.env.local

# Documentation builds
site/
docs/_build/
